# The interpreter remembers what a name that is not a local stands for, so a
# run works the ladder out once per name instead of on every evaluation. That
# is sound only because a non-local name means ONE thing for a whole run, and
# these two refusals are what make it so: a parameter may not be spelled like
# a declaration in the same module, nor like a builtin. Relax either and a
# spelling could mean the declaration in one frame and a binding in the next,
# which is the case a remembered answer cannot see.
#
# The environment is still asked first, before the memory, so the ordering
# does not rest on this file. What rests on it is that there is nothing for
# the ordering to protect.
fn inc n
  n + 1

fn shade inc
  inc * 10

fn shadier length
  length * 10

pub play = print "x"
